      <title>Relocation of Cape Town baboons to sanctuary ignites heated protests</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/cape-town-baboons-relocation-protests</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Demonstrators tried to block vehicle carrying the baboons, whose capture authorities say is needed to protect both primate and human&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The relocation of a troop of baboons in Cape Town to a wildlife sanctuary has triggered furious protests by local people opposed to their capture, which officials argue is necessary to stop human-wildlife conflict in the city.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 44-member Waterfall troop (named after the area they mainly inhabit) was captured in the southern seaside suburb of Simon’s Town on Friday and Saturday. A second, smaller Seaforth troop is also due to be moved.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/cape-town-baboons-relocation-protests"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
